Open a shell (or run a command) inside a workspace

Usage: forkspace enter [OPTIONS] [NAME] [-- <COMMAND>...]

Arguments:
  [NAME]        Name of the workspace to enter (omit to auto-detect)
  [COMMAND]...  Command to run inside the workspace instead of a shell

Options:
      --create             Create the workspace if it does not exist
      --from <FROM>        Base directory when creating a new workspace on entry
      --ephemeral          Destroy the workspace automatically on exit
      --tmpfs              Keep the workspace's changes in RAM (Linux overlay only; lost on reboot)
      --copy               Consent to a full directory copy backend when creating
      --live               When creating, show later changes to the base in the workspace (Linux overlay only)
      --no-sandbox         Let the shell or command write outside the workspace
      --sandbox-info       List where commands in the workspace may write, then exit
      --merge-on-exit      Merge changes back to the base directory when exiting the shell
      --session <SESSION>  Session identifier to set in the spawned shell
  -h, --help               Print help
